# build intermediates (the c2go pipeline)
*.bc
*.o
*.tmp
/build/
/cmake-build-*/
/_tmp/

# musl is a LOCAL symlink (-> ../musl) for now; becomes a git submodule at push time.
/musl

# c2go-clang-GENERATED bindings: NOT tracked during the migration (they change on every
# regen). Regenerate with ./gen.sh; add + commit them all at once at the END.
/libc_*_*.go
/libc_*_*.s
# selftest/ holds ONLY generated bindings + hand-written *_test.go (+ source/*.c),
# so ignore structurally rather than by generated basename (which gen.sh could
# rename): every .s is generated (hand-written asm lives at the root), and every
# non-test .go is a generated binding.
/selftest/*.s
/selftest/*.go
!/selftest/*_test.go

# working migration notes — kept local, not tracked.
/MIGRATION_PLAN.md

# NOTE: hand-written *.go (Go glue) + *_test.go at the root ARE tracked (shipped source).
# csrc/ has its own go.mod (nested module) so its *.c stay out of the module zip.

# local / editor / tooling
.codex-gpt-session-id
.DS_Store

# never track local portability notes (see LICENSING_PLAN_A)
PORTABILITY.md
